From: songhyunho1111 <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Subject: ipc/msg: keep expelled receivers from taking new messages
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:28:21 +0900

Patch series "ipc/msg: prevent reads after queue permission revocation".

Two races can let a blocked msgrcv() obtain a message sent after IPC_SET
revoked its read permission.  Patch 1 prevents a sender from handing a
message to a receiver that IPC_SET has asked to retry.  Patch 2 makes the
receive permission check atomic with insertion into the receiver list. 
Messages handed off before IPC_SET takes the queue lock retain their
existing behavior.


This patch (of 2):

IPC_SET wakes blocked receivers to recheck read permission, but
expunge_all() leaves them in q_receivers.  Before a receiver runs,
pipelined_send() can replace its -EAGAIN result with a new message.  The
receiver can then obtain data sent after its read access was revoked.

Mark receivers touched by expunge_all() and skip them in pipelined_send().
Leave them on the list until they wake: IPC_RMID must still find them and
change -EAGAIN to -EIDRM before the queue can be freed.  A skipped message
remains on the queue for an authorized receiver.  The resumed receiver
removes itself from the list and retries its permission check.

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Manfred Spraul <manfred@colorfullife.com>
Cc: Davidlohr Bueso <dave@stgolabs.net>
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>

 ipc/msg.c |    7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/ipc/msg.c~ipc-msg-keep-expelled-receivers-from-taking-new-messages
+++ a/ipc/msg.c
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ struct msg_receiver {
 	long			r_maxsize;
 
 	struct msg_msg		*r_msg;
+	bool			r_expunge;
 };
 
 /* one msg_sender for each sleeping sender */
@@ -255,6 +256,8 @@ static void expunge_all(struct msg_queue
 		struct task_struct *r_tsk;
 
 		r_tsk = get_task_struct(msr->r_tsk);
+		/* IPC_RMID must still find this waiter and set -EIDRM. */
+		msr->r_expunge = true;
 
 		/* see MSG_BARRIER for purpose/pairing */
 		smp_store_release(&msr->r_msg, ERR_PTR(res));
@@ -817,6 +820,9 @@ static inline int pipelined_send(struct
 	struct msg_receiver *msr, *t;
 
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(msr, t, &msq->q_receivers, r_list) {
+		/* IPC_SET needs the receiver to recheck its access. */
+		if (msr->r_expunge)
+			continue;
 		if (testmsg(msg, msr->r_msgtype, msr->r_mode) &&
 		    !security_msg_queue_msgrcv(&msq->q_perm, msg, msr->r_tsk,
 					       msr->r_msgtype, msr->r_mode)) {
@@ -1176,6 +1182,7 @@ static long do_msgrcv(int msqid, void __
 			goto out_unlock0;
 		}
 
+		msr_d.r_expunge = false;
 		list_add_tail(&msr_d.r_list, &msq->q_receivers);
 		msr_d.r_tsk = current;
 		msr_d.r_msgtype = msgtyp;
_
